==Battleground==
*5 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Coffin Zoge]] spawns.
*1 [[Zigge]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Zigge]]s spawn, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**50 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
**4 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Zamelle]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This is a fairly average zombie stage, with Gravey and Zamelle acting as the backliners while Zigge and Zang Roo act as the main pushers.

Zigge is not a particularly large threat due to it being killed rather easily by [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. Zang Roo can prove to be annoying with its high bulk, along with them being spawned frequently such that Holy Blast will not be able to unburrow all of them.

Bring units that can counter the two Zang Roos that will slip past your frontline, by having them be able to outrange and preferably Z-Kill them. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] and even [[Trash Cat (Special Cat)|Trash Cat]] will prove useful here. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] will be your main line of defense, especially when boosted with a few research combos.

